language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Place m oranges in n bowls on a line, at most one orange per bowl, with no three oranges in arithmetic progression. Print the bowls used in ascending order.
given n : int(1..)
given m : int(1..)
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..m)] of int(1..n)

branching on [x]

such that
$ the oranges are listed in ascending bowl order, which also makes every bowl hold at most one orange
forAll i : int(1..m-1) . x[i] < x[i+1],
$ no three oranges A, B, C (in bowl order) have the distance A-B equal to the distance B-C, i.e. no A+C = 2B
forAll i : int(1..m) . forAll j : int(i+1..m) . forAll k : int(j+1..m) . x[i] + x[k] != 2 * x[j]
